ventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA EIICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEDA, KENJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWASAKI, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUBO, DAIRI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MINOGUCHI, RYO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, EISHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA, EIICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A gas generator composition which contains a nitrogenous organic compound effective in eliminating the harmfulness problem of conventional metal azide compounds, and which accomplishes the inconsistent subjects of prevention of the generation of harmful gases such as Nox and CO and capture of slug and further eliminates problems of conventional autoignition mechanisms. The composition comprises a fuel ingredient, an oxidizing agent, and a catalyst ingredient as major ingredients, wherein the fuel ingredient is 20 to 45 wt.% aminotetrazole, the oxidizing agent is contained in an amount of 50 to 75 wt.%, and the catalyst ingredient is 0.05 to 5 wt.% molybdenum trioxide, serving to impart autoignitability.  The oxidizing agent comprises strontium nitrate and the nitrate or perchlorate of either an alkali metal or barium and has a strontium nitrate content of 75 to 95 wt.%.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur une composition génératrice de gaz renfermant un composé organique azoté efficace pour éliminer le caractère nocif des composés d'azoture. Cette composition a pour effet de prévenir la génération de gaz nocifs tels que Nox et CO et permet d'éliminer les obturations et autres problèmes d'auto-allumage généralement rencontrés. La composition de cette invention comprend comme ingrédients principaux, un ingrédient de combustible, un agent d'oxydation et un ingrédient de catalyseur, l'ingrédient de combustible étant un aminotétrazole compris entre 20 et 45 % en poids, l'agent d'oxydation étant compris entre 50 et 75 % en poids et l'ingrédient de catalyseur étant un trioxyde de molybdène compris entre 0,05 et 5 % en poids, qui permettent de conférer une capacité d'auto-allumage. L'agent d'oxydation comprend un nitrate de strontium et le nitrate ou perchlorate d'un métal alcalin ou de baryum et présente une teneur en nitrate de strontium comprise entre 75 et 95 % en poids.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>